{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Composition","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix_of_isSemisimpleRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix_of_isSemisimpleRing","kind":"instance","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.lean#L36-L60","doc":"**`IsSemisimpleRing (Matrix m m R)` for a general semisimple base** —\nMathlib's `proof_wanted IsSemisimpleRing.matrix`, in full.\n\n`MatrixSemisimple.instIsSemisimpleRing_matrix` covers the **division-ring**\nbase. This lifts it to any semisimple `R`, by composing pieces that all already\nexist:\n\n1. Artin–Wedderburn (`exists_ringEquiv_pi_matrix_divisionRing`) writes\n   `R ≃+* Π i, Matrix (Fin (d i)) (Fin (d i)) (D i)` over division rings `D i`;\n2. `RingEquiv.mapMatrix` carries that inside `Matrix m m`;\n3. `matrixPiRingEquiv` pushes the product outwards;\n4. `Matrix.compRingEquiv` flattens each `Matrix m m (Matrix _ _ (D i))` to\n   `Matrix (m × Fin (d i)) (m × Fin (d i)) (D i)`, semisimple by the\n   division-ring case;\n5. a finite product of semisimple rings is semisimple, and\n   `RingEquiv.isSemisimpleRing` transports back along the composite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.matrixPiRingEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.matrixPiRingEquiv","kind":"def","line":9,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MatrixSemisimpleGeneral.lean#L9-L34","doc":"**Matrices over a product ring are the product of the matrix rings.**\n\n`Matrix m m (Π i, S i) ≃+* Π i, Matrix m m (S i)`. A transposition of the two\nouter indices; every field is `rfl` except multiplicativity. Mathlib has\n`Matrix.compRingEquiv` for matrices *of* matrices but nothing for matrices over\na `Pi`.\n\nThe `Matrix.of` in `toFun` is load-bearing, not decoration. `Matrix m m α` is a\ntype synonym for `m → m → α`, so a bare `fun a b => …` elaborates with the **Pi**\nmultiplication (`instHMul` on `m → m → S i`) even under a\n`: Matrix m m (S i)` ascription — and then `Matrix.mul_apply` does not fire,\nwhile `Pi.mul_apply` fires and rewrites the product pointwise, which is the\nwrong lemma. `Matrix.of` pins the matrix structure. ","signatureChunk":0}]}